  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-value first experiment is to establish a simple, well-understood baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal RNA-only configuration: it uses a standard linear dimensionality reduction (PCA to 2000 dims) and a single profile, avoiding confounds from learned encoders, multi-profile aggregation, or fusion. This gives a clean reference accuracy for RNA signal alone. In experiment 2 I can then test the image-only counterpart (e.g., config_010) to determine which modality carries more signal, and from there decide whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion, better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), or multiprofile aggregation. Starting from the simplest baseline reduces uncertainty about the fundamental contribution of each modality before adding complexity."
}

